From df2148c9c8b8ea6af586eeef5bedaf3a648fa357 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:31:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(draw): configurable two-team draw generation (Stage
 3, C2)

- New types: OddBracketMethod, PairingMethod, ConflictAvoidance,
  PullupRestriction, plus TournamentPreferences fields for each, and
  repeatMatchupPenalty/institutionClashPenalty (BP).
- src/lib/draw/pairing.ts: pairTeams() implements slide, fold, adjacent,
  random, and fold_top_adjacent_rest (fold the top room, adjacent for the
  rest) over an already-ranked, even-length team list.
- src/lib/draw/oddBrackets.ts: resolveOddBrackets() implements all 6 odd-
  bracket methods (pullup_top/bottom/middle/random, intermediate,
  intermediate_bubble), composed with pullupRestriction (none/least_pulled/
  lowest_draw_strength_speaks/lowest_draw_strength_wins) which narrows the
  candidate pool before the method picks a position within it. Cascading
  pull-ups (pulling from a bracket can leave it odd, needing its own pull)
  are handled correctly, including skipping over brackets that are
  legitimately empty when finding 'the bracket below'.
- src/lib/draw/conflictAvoidance.ts: avoidConflicts() implements off,
  one_up_one_down (cheap local swap pass) and min_cost (reuses the existing
  Hungarian matcher, framing the bracket as a bipartite matching between its
  top and bottom half).
- src/lib/draw/twoTeamDraw.ts: generateTwoTeamDraw() composes all of the
  above in the specified order -- raw brackets by wins -> resolve odd
  brackets -> pair within brackets -> avoid conflicts -> allocate sides --
  and reads standings.metrics (from C1) for pullupRestriction and wins
  grouping, tying C1 and C2 together as intended.
- powerPaired.ts (BP): calculateDebateClashPenalty's hardcoded 1000/200
  penalties are now parameters, defaulting to the same values, sourced from
  the new preferences in generator.ts.
- generator.ts: routes BP through the existing (now configurable-penalty)
  power-paired generator, and two-team formats through the new pipeline.
- Config page: new 'Draw Generation' card (BP: penalty inputs; two-team:
  the four C2 dropdowns).
- Tests: 66 new (pairing 10, oddBrackets 35 incl. a 300-iteration x 24
  method/restriction-combo property test, conflictAvoidance 7, twoTeamDraw 7,
  plus 2 more on the existing powerPaired suite for configurable BP
  penalties -- an exhaustive-combination test caught a real cascading-pullup
  bug (only checking the literal next bracket instead of the next non-empty
  one) before it shipped. All 120 tests pass; the 47 tests from before C1/C2
  are unaffected.
